1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,300
One population does not necessarily mean one set

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:03,940
of needs.

3
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:07,820
Averages can hide differences between patients, customers and

4
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:08,400
communities.

5
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:11,217
Clustering helps us explore those differences.

6
00:00:11,877 --> 00:00:14,577
Supervised learning uses labelled examples to learn a

7
00:00:14,577 --> 00:00:14,977
target.

8
00:00:15,737 --> 00:00:18,797
Unsupervised learning explores data without those target labels.

9
00:00:19,437 --> 00:00:21,277
Clustering groups similar observations.

10
00:00:21,797 --> 00:00:23,677
The profiles depend on what we measure.

11
00:00:24,377 --> 00:00:27,557
K-means assigns observations to the nearest centre, then

12
00:00:27,557 --> 00:00:29,657
updates each centre to its group mean.

13
00:00:30,337 --> 00:00:32,077
It needs a chosen number of clusters and

14
00:00:32,077 --> 00:00:34,457
favours compact, roughly spherical groups.

15
00:00:34,917 --> 00:00:37,957
Agglomerative clustering merges observations into nested groups.

16
00:00:38,297 --> 00:00:39,797
A dendrogram shows the hierarchy.

17
00:00:40,537 --> 00:00:43,157
Cophenetic correlation checks how well its merge distances

18
00:00:43,157 --> 00:00:46,417
reflect the original distances; it does not establish

19
00:00:46,417 --> 00:00:47,577
meaningful profiles.

20
00:00:48,217 --> 00:00:52,937
Explore missingness, then clean, encode and scale thoughtfully.

21
00:00:52,937 --> 00:00:56,337
PCA can simplify the feature space, but may

22
00:00:56,337 --> 00:00:57,757
discard useful structure.

23
00:00:58,317 --> 00:01:01,537
Compare candidate cluster counts using silhouette scores, stability

24
00:01:01,877 --> 00:01:02,837
and domain knowledge.

25
00:01:03,377 --> 00:01:05,597
Interpret profiles using original variables.

26
00:01:06,337 --> 00:01:09,279
In my published Nigerian HIV research, we analysed

27
00:01:09,279 --> 00:01:11,957
eleven thousand five hundred and eighty-nine records reported

28
00:01:11,957 --> 00:01:13,891
as lost to follow-up across three hundred and

29
00:01:13,891 --> 00:01:17,117
thirteen USAID and PEPFAR-supported clinics.

30
00:01:17,937 --> 00:01:20,477
Hierarchical clustering identified six profiles.

31
00:01:20,477 --> 00:01:24,117
This described differences; it did not establish causes

32
00:01:24,117 --> 00:01:25,417
or intervention effects.

33
00:01:26,237 --> 00:01:30,137
Profiles can inform hypotheses about treatment-continuity support, customer

34
00:01:30,137 --> 00:01:32,197
journeys and financial-service needs.

35
00:01:32,737 --> 00:01:35,217
Validate those ideas with people who use the

36
00:01:35,217 --> 00:01:35,757
services.

37
00:01:36,617 --> 00:01:39,157
Clusters describe patterns, not causes.

38
00:01:39,677 --> 00:01:42,237
Test tailored responses and evaluate equity.

39
00:01:43,017 --> 00:01:43,337
EvidenceLab.

40
00:01:43,897 --> 00:01:44,197
See it.

41
00:01:44,577 --> 00:01:45,337
Understand it.

42
00:01:45,757 --> 00:01:46,137
Run it.